From: DevElderLost
Subject: [PATCH] xwayland: DRI3 without DRM (wl_shm + optional linux-dmabuf zero-copy)

Xwayland only exposes DRI3 through glamor/GBM, which needs a DRM render
node. Without /dev/dri (proot on Android) clients get no DRI3 at all.

Register DRI3 1.2 on the plain wl_shm path when glamor is unavailable:
 - DRI3Open is refused, only DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR is advertised
 - PixmapFromBuffers mmap()s the client's dma-buf as pixmap storage,
   so Present can always copy it (DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC around CPU reads)
 - if the compositor offers linux-dmabuf with LINEAR for the format, a
   wl_buffer is also created asynchronously so Present can flip with
   zero copies; on failure the copy path is kept
 - env XWL_NODRM_DRI3=0 disables, XWL_NODRM_DRI3_ZEROCOPY=0 copy only,
   XWL_NODRM_DRI3_DEBUG=1 traces buffers and counts copies vs flips

Base: xwayland 24.1.6 (Debian trixie). Apply with: patch -p1
---
diff -urN -x build xwayland-24.1.6.orig/hw/xwayland/meson.build xwayland-24.1.6/hw/xwayland/meson.build
--- a/hw/xwayland/meson.build
+++ b/hw/xwayland/meson.build
@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@
     'xwayland-cursor.h',
     'xwayland-drm-lease.h',
     'xwayland-drm-lease.c',
+    'xwayland-dri3-nodrm.c',
+    'xwayland-dri3-nodrm.h',
     'xwayland-glamor.h',
     'xwayland-pixmap.c',
     'xwayland-pixmap.h',
diff -urN -x build xwayland-24.1.6.orig/hw/xwayland/xwayland-dri3-nodrm.c xwayland-24.1.6/hw/xwayland/xwayland-dri3-nodrm.c
